config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_DSVT
	bool "Domoticz plugin: DSVT zone heating/cooling control"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_MOD_SQLITE
	default n
	help
		DSVT is a multi-zone heating, cooling and domestic hot water
		control system for Domoticz: up to 12 zones with individual room
		thermostats (or TRV valves), several heat sources (heat pump,
		boiler, electric heater), floor/radiator/wall/ceiling emitters,
		per-zone door and window detection, and a dashboard page served
		by the Domoticz web server.

		Unlike a plain thermostat script it creates the whole device tree
		and the control logic itself, and it keeps its state in a small
		SQLite database (hence the selected Python sqlite3 module); the
		Duinzicht/MiHome style viewers are not required.

		The plugin uses the Domoticz module and the Python standard
		library, and its labels follow the language of the hardware entry
		(16 translations; the dashboard page brings its own set).

		Setup: Setup -> Hardware -> add the DSVT hardware, then open the
		DSVT setup page of the plugin (linked from the hardware page) to
		define zones and heat sources.

		Licensed MIT upstream (LICENSE is installed with the plugin). The
		repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a pinned
		commit of the main branch.
